---
interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className = "legal-article" } = Astro.props;
---
<article class={className}>
  <p>
    <strong>Jason Holt Digital LLC</strong> publishes Tome Keeper and is the data controller for it. For any privacy
    question, email <a href="mailto:ryan@jasonholtdigital.com">ryan@jasonholtdigital.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The Short Version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Tome Keeper has no accounts and never asks for your name, email address or phone number.</li>
    <li>Your PDFs, bookmarks, page tags, sets, Tables, clips and settings stay on your device unless you turn on iCloud Sync, Google Drive Sync or OneDrive Sync. Synced library data goes only to your own private iCloud account, Google Drive or OneDrive. Jason Holt Digital does not receive or store it.</li>
    <li>There are no ads, no analytics and no tracking. I don't sell data.</li>
    <li>Diagnostics are on so I can fix errors and slow screens. You can turn them off in Settings, under Diagnostics.</li>
    <li>The app checks for fixes when it starts and while it's open.</li>
    <li>If you connect DriveThruRPG, the app talks to DriveThruRPG directly. I never see your key or your purchases.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What This Policy Covers</h2>
  <p>This policy applies to Tome Keeper on iPhone, iPad, Mac, Windows and Android, including beta versions from TestFlight and Google Play and the Windows version from the Microsoft Store.</p>
  <p>iCloud Sync is available on iPhone, iPad and Mac. Google Drive Sync is available on Android. OneDrive Sync is available on Windows.</p>

  <h2>What Stays on Your Device</h2>
  <p>
    The PDFs you import are copied into Tome Keeper's storage on your device. Your library, sets, bookmarks, page tags,
    Tables, clips and settings are stored there too. If you turn on iCloud Sync, Google Drive Sync or OneDrive Sync, the
    library data described below also goes to your own private iCloud account, Google Drive or OneDrive. On iPhone, iPad and Mac, your device's own backups may include this data,
    depending on your backup settings.
  </p>

  <h2>What the App Sends</h2>

  <h3>iCloud Sync (Only If You Turn It On)</h3>
  <p>
    iCloud Sync is optional and off by default on each device. On iPhone, iPad and Mac, you can turn it on in Tome Keeper's
    Settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    It syncs library data, including book details and covers, sets, bookmarks, reading positions, page tags, shared
    settings, and Tables with their clips, notes, images and attached PDFs. Book PDF files also upload when
    <strong>Sync book files</strong> is on. That switch starts on when you first enable iCloud Sync; you can turn it off
    separately. Book PDFs download on your other devices when you open them.
  </p>
  <p>
    This data goes directly between your devices and the private CloudKit database in your own iCloud account. Jason Holt
    Digital does not receive, store or have access to your synced library data. Apple provides iCloud under its
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    To stop syncing on a device, turn off <strong>iCloud Sync</strong> in Tome Keeper's Settings. Turning it off, or
    uninstalling Tome Keeper, does not delete copies already in iCloud or on your other devices.
  </p>

  <h3>Google Drive Sync (Only If You Turn It On)</h3>
  <p>
    Google Drive Sync is optional and off by default on each device. On Android, you can turn it on in Tome Keeper's
    Settings. Google then asks you to choose a Google account and to let Tome Keeper use its own app data folder in that
    account's Google Drive.
  </p>
  <p>
    It syncs the same library data as iCloud Sync. Book PDF files also upload when <strong>Sync book files</strong> is
    on, and on Android they upload only on Wi-Fi. Book PDFs download on your other devices when you open them.
  </p>
  <p>
    This data goes directly between your devices and a hidden app data folder in your own Google Drive, over an encrypted
    connection. Tome Keeper can open only that folder, not your other Drive files. Jason Holt Digital does not receive,
    store or have access to your synced library data. Google provides Google Drive under its
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>, and the
    data counts toward your Google storage.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tome Keeper keeps the email address of the account you chose on your device to show it in Settings. It is not synced
    or sent to me.
  </p>
  <p>
    To stop syncing on a device, turn off <strong>Google Drive Sync</strong> in Tome Keeper's Settings. This also signs
    Tome Keeper out of Google. Turning it off, or uninstalling Tome Keeper, does not delete copies already in your Google
    Drive or on your other devices.
  </p>

  <h3>OneDrive Sync (Only If You Turn It On)</h3>
  <p>
    OneDrive Sync is optional and off by default on each device. On Windows, you can turn it on in Tome Keeper's
    Settings. Your browser then opens Microsoft's sign-in page, where you choose a personal Microsoft account and let
    Tome Keeper use its own app folder in that account's OneDrive.
  </p>
  <p>
    It syncs the same library data as iCloud Sync. Book PDF files also upload when <strong>Sync book files</strong> is
    on. Book PDFs download on your other devices when you open them.
  </p>
  <p>
    This data goes directly between your devices and the Tome Keeper folder inside the Apps folder of your own
    OneDrive, over an encrypted connection. Tome Keeper can open only that folder, not your other OneDrive files. Jason
    Holt Digital does not receive, store or have access to your synced library data. Microsoft provides OneDrive under
    its <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/privacy/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy
    statement</a>, and the data counts toward your OneDrive storage.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tome Keeper keeps the email address of the account you chose, and a sign-in token that lets it keep syncing without
    asking you to sign in again, on your PC. The token is encrypted in Windows' secure storage. Neither is synced or sent
    to me.
  </p>
  <p>
    To stop syncing on a device, turn off <strong>OneDrive Sync</strong> in Tome Keeper's Settings. This also signs
    Tome Keeper out of your Microsoft account on that PC. Turning it off, or uninstalling Tome Keeper, does not delete
    copies already in your OneDrive or on your other devices.
  </p>

  <h3>Diagnostics</h3>  <p>
    When an error happens in Tome Keeper's own code, the app sends a report to Sentry so I can find and fix it. A report
    contains:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the type of error and where it happened in the app's code, by file name and line;</li>
    <li>the app version, build and update number;</li>
    <li>your device model, processor type, memory, screen size, battery level and whether you're online;</li>
    <li>your operating system and its version;</li>
    <li>
      which kinds of screens you opened just before, such as the library or a book. A report names the kind of screen,
      never the book or Table.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    With diagnostics on, the app also sends how long it takes to start, open screens and load a PDF, how smoothly screens
    draw, and whether a session ended in an error, so I can see which versions are stable and fast.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reports carry a random ID for your installation, so I can tell one installation hitting a bug many times from many
    installations hitting it once. That ID isn't connected to you or to anything that identifies you.
  </p>
  <p>
    On iPhone, iPad and Mac, a crash inside the app's own native code sends a smaller report with the same app, device and
    system details.
  </p>
  <p>
    Diagnostics are on from the start. To turn them off, open Settings and switch off <strong>Share diagnostics</strong>
    under Diagnostics. The app stops sending at once.
  </p>

  <h3>Updates</h3>
  <p>
    When the app starts, and every 30 minutes while it's open, it asks Shorebird whether a fix is available for your
    version and downloads it if there is one. The request includes the app's ID and version, your platform and processor
    type, the fix number you already have, and a random ID that Shorebird's updater creates for your installation.
    Shorebird uses that ID only to count installations.
  </p>

  <h3>DriveThruRPG (Only If You Connect It)</h3>
  <p>
    You can import PDFs you bought on DriveThruRPG. To do that, you enter your own DriveThruRPG API key in Tome Keeper.
    The app sends it to DriveThruRPG, receives a sign-in token, and keeps both in your device's secure storage (the
    Keychain on Apple devices). The app then asks DriveThruRPG for your purchased titles and downloads the PDFs you
    choose.
  </p>
  <p>
    These requests go straight from your device to DriveThruRPG. I never receive your key, your token or your purchase
    list. DriveThruRPG handles them under its
    <a href="https://www.drivethrurpg.com/privacy.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">own privacy policy</a>.
    Disconnecting DriveThruRPG in Tome Keeper deletes the stored key and token from your device.
  </p>

  <h3>Links in Your PDFs</h3>
  <p>
    When you tap a web link inside a PDF, Tome Keeper asks first, then opens it in your browser. The website you open
    handles your visit under its own policy.
  </p>

  <h3>What the App Never Sends</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your PDFs, their file names or their titles, except to your own private iCloud account, Google Drive or OneDrive if you turn on sync. Book PDF uploads also require Sync book files.</li>
    <li>Bookmarks, page tags, notes, set names, Table contents or clips, except to your own private iCloud account, Google Drive or OneDrive if you turn on sync</li>
    <li>Screenshots or recordings of your screen</li>
    <li>Your name, email address or phone number</li>
    <li>Your exact location</li>
    <li>Your advertising ID</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who Receives Data</h2>
  <p>
    Sentry processes diagnostics on my behalf under a data processing agreement, and only for the purposes in this policy.
    Shorebird handles update data under its own privacy policy.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Sentry</strong> receives diagnostics. These records are stored in the United States; Sentry lists Google
      Cloud and Amazon Web Services as its hosting providers. Transfers rely on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and
      Standard Contractual Clauses. Error events and session data are kept for 30 days on Sentry's free plan and for 90
      days on its Team and Business plans.
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://sentry.io/legal/subprocessors/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Subprocessors</a></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shorebird</strong> (updates). Runs on Google Cloud in Iowa, United States, and delivers fixes from Google
      Cloud Storage. Shorebird keeps installation counts as anonymous tallies rather than a list of IDs.
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://shorebird.dev/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://docs.shorebird.dev/system/security/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Security</a></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>DriveThruRPG</strong>, only if you connect it, as described above.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Apple (iCloud)</strong> stores your synced library data in your own private iCloud account, only if you turn
      on iCloud Sync, under its
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google (Google Drive)</strong> stores your synced library data in your own Google Drive, only if you turn on
      Google Drive Sync, under its
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Microsoft (OneDrive)</strong> stores your synced library data in your own OneDrive, only if you turn on
      OneDrive Sync, under its
      <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/privacy/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you get Tome Keeper from the App Store, TestFlight, Google Play or the Microsoft Store, that store handles your download under its own
    privacy policy. Your device's operating system may also send crash information to Apple, Google or Microsoft, depending on your
    device settings. Those companies decide how they use it, not me.
  </p>

  <h2>I Don't Sell Your Data</h2>
  <p>
    I don't sell or share personal information for advertising, I don't use targeted advertising, and I don't work with
    data brokers.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>iCloud Sync:</strong> Settings, iCloud Sync. Off until you turn it on, separately on each iPhone, iPad or Mac. Sync book files controls book PDF uploads.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Drive Sync:</strong> Settings, Google Drive Sync. Off until you turn it on, separately on each Android device. Sync book files controls book PDF uploads.</li>
    <li><strong>OneDrive Sync:</strong> Settings, OneDrive Sync. Off until you turn it on, separately on each Windows PC. Sync book files controls book PDF uploads.</li>
    <li><strong>Diagnostics:</strong> Settings, Diagnostics, Share diagnostics. On until you turn them off.</li>
    <li><strong>DriveThruRPG:</strong> off until you connect it. Disconnect it at any time to delete the stored key and token.</li>
    <li><strong>Your device:</strong> your operating system's settings control what it shares with Apple, Google or Microsoft.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal Basis (GDPR)</h2>
  <p>For people in the European Union and the United Kingdom, I rely on:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Providing the service you asked for:</strong> delivering updates, connecting to DriveThruRPG when you ask, and syncing with your own iCloud account, Google Drive or OneDrive when you turn on sync.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> diagnostics, so I can keep the app working. You can object at any time by turning them off in Settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Replying to you:</strong> when you email me.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your Privacy Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, privacy laws may give you rights to access, correct, delete, export, restrict, or object
    to processing of your personal information, and to complain to a privacy regulator.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your synced library data is in your own iCloud account, Google Drive or OneDrive. You can delete Tome Keeper's iCloud data through your device's
    iCloud storage settings. You can delete Tome Keeper's Google Drive data in Google Drive on the web: open Settings,
    then Manage apps, find Tome Keeper, open Options and choose Delete hidden app data. You can delete Tome Keeper's
    OneDrive data by deleting its folder inside the Apps folder of your OneDrive, and remove its access to your
    Microsoft account in your Microsoft account's privacy settings, under apps that can access your data. Jason Holt Digital cannot retrieve or delete those private copies for you. Keep copies of
    anything you want to save before deleting it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Diagnostics can't be matched to you, by design: they carry a random installation ID that the app doesn't show you,
    so I can't find one person's reports. Turning diagnostics off stops new reports, and existing reports expire from
    Sentry within 90 days.
  </p>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:ryan@jasonholtdigital.com">ryan@jasonholtdigital.com</a> with your request. I'll respond within
    the time the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Tome Keeper is not directed to children under 13. It doesn't require an account or ask for a birth date, so I don't know
    a reader's age. If you believe a child has sent personal information through the app or a support email, write to
    <a href="mailto:ryan@jasonholtdigital.com">ryan@jasonholtdigital.com</a> so I can review and delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    When I change this policy, I'll update the date at the top. If a change affects what the app sends, I'll say so in the
    app's release notes.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Me</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:ryan@jasonholtdigital.com">ryan@jasonholtdigital.com</a>, or write to Jason Holt Digital LLC,
    1111b S Governors Avenue STE 21904, Dover, DE 19904, USA.
  </p>
</article>
